That would depend how you shutdown. If you type: shutdown -h now (to a 
halt), no shutdown scripts are ever used; Tru64 simply shuts down.  
However is you type: shutdown now (to single user mode), your script 
should work.

Tru64 UNIX 5.1B has another flag to invoke stop scripts when shutting 
down: -s. If you type: shutdown -sh now, your script should work.

You have tested your script by typing: /sbin/init.d/script1 start and 
/sbin/init.d/script1 stop, I presume?

