 You compile the software and place it first in the library_path.  All
 it does is log all the calls to execv and execve and then call the
 correct symbol in the C library.
 
 In Linux it works perfectlly, but when I try tu use it in Tru64 all
 I get is: seg fault.  The Linux/Solaris Makefile uses de '-ldl' flag,
 on Tru64 it doesn't work.  I'm using gcc-3.2.2 20030222.
 
