Some kind person helped my out.  His advice was:

>>>boot -fl s -fi "/genvmunix"
# bcheckrc
# doconfig
# cp /vmunix /vmunix.some.unique.value
# cp /sys/HOSTNAME/vmunix /
# reboot

This worked almost exactly as described except for doconfig looking
for mkdir and uname in /bin instead of /usr/bin, where they were. 
Copying them to /bin allowed doconfig to rebuild the kernel and when
the system rebooted, all was well.  Thanks to Alan Rollow.
