What do you mean by recursive acl rights?  Can you give an
example?

You can set a Default Directory ACL and/or a Default Access
ACL on a directory so that the ACL inherited by all directories
and/or file created in the directory.  There is information on this
in the Security manual.

You can set an Access ACL on a directory so that access to
all of the contents of that directory is permitted or denied.

You cannot set an ACL on a directory that will propagate itself
to all of the existing files and subdirectories in that directory.

Ann




