The debugger says that program was executing in the pthread_kill 
function when it got an abort. This particular logic tests to see if a thread
(a communication thread to clients) is in fact valid before attempting to
queue an update packet to the thread to be sent down to a client. The client
could have shitdown which would cause the thread to be deleted. Other threads
receive data packets from other applications in the server and 
queue them to the communication threads where theya re transmitted to the
client using CORBA middle ware. We need to be
able to reliably determine if the communication thread is still available
for use which is why we are calling pthread_kill(thread_id, 0) 


